# Written once by `nidoo init-bundled`; edit freely, it is never overwritten.
# Mosquitto reads it at start and on SIGHUP: `docker compose kill -s HUP mosquitto`.
#
# Every user keeps full access, as before this file existed: the hub's own login,
# and any login you added for Zigbee2MQTT or another client. Mosquitto logs a
# harmless warning at start because these patterns name no %u or %c.
pattern readwrite #
pattern read $SYS/#

# The phone app's login, which travels in the setup QR. A deny wins over the
# grants above, so whoever reads the QR cannot send alerts to every phone,
# change the alarm settings or the flow labels, or read the broker's own log.
user nidoo-app
topic deny nidoo/push/notification/#
topic deny nidoo/alarm/settings
topic deny nidoo/flow_labels
topic deny $SYS/#
